1
00:00:05,690 --> 00:00:10,680
The Moon is about 384,400 kilometres from Earth.

2
00:00:10,730 --> 00:00:16,460
A news report gives numbers with just 2 important digits, to make them easy to read.

3
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:19,560
These are called significant figures.

4
00:00:19,610 --> 00:00:22,960
What is 384,400 to 2 significant figures?

5
00:00:23,010 --> 00:00:26,600
Pause the video and try it.

6
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:29,540
The two most important digits are 3 and 8.

7
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:32,550
The next digit is 4, so we do not round up.

8
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:36,950
Then fill the other places with zeros to keep the size.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,880
384,400 to 2 significant figures is 380,000 kilometres.

10
00:00:43,930 --> 00:00:46,650
Remember how to round to decimal places.

11
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,240
Look at the next digit.

12
00:00:48,290 --> 00:00:50,800
If it is 5 or more, round up.

13
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:57,500
3.476 to 2 decimal places: the next digit is 6, so round up to 3.48.

14
00:00:57,550 --> 00:01:01,140
Significant figures are the digits that matter most.

15
00:01:01,190 --> 00:01:05,260
Start counting at the first digit that is not zero.

16
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:09,240
In 384,400 the first significant figure is 3.

17
00:01:09,290 --> 00:01:13,390
In 0.0712, the zeros at the front do not count.

18
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:16,950
The first significant figure is 7.

19
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,960
Zeros between other digits do count.

20
00:01:20,010 --> 00:01:26,680
5.096 to 2 significant figures is 5.1, because the 9 makes the 0 round up.

21
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:27,500
Your turn.

22
00:01:27,550 --> 00:01:31,240
How many significant figures does 0.0405 have?

23
00:01:31,290 --> 00:01:34,830
Pause the video and try it.

24
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:37,780
The zeros at the front do not count.

25
00:01:37,830 --> 00:01:39,000
Start at the 4.

26
00:01:39,050 --> 00:01:40,230
Then 0, then 5.

27
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:43,500
The zero between the 4 and the 5 counts.

28
00:01:43,550 --> 00:01:47,000
So 0.0405 has 3 significant figures.

29
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:55,090
When you round a large number, fill the places after the last significant figure with zeros.

30
00:01:55,140 --> 00:02:00,210
384,400 to 2 significant figures is 380,000, not 38.

31
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:05,020
For decimals, do not add zeros after the rounded digit.

32
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:09,590
0.0712 to 2 significant figures is just 0.071.

33
00:02:09,640 --> 00:02:10,930
Here is the method.

34
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:14,170
Step 1: find the first digit that is not zero.

35
00:02:14,220 --> 00:02:17,320
That is the first significant figure.

36
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:22,630
Step 2: count along to the number of significant figures you need.

37
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,870
Step 3: look at the next digit.

38
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:27,230
5 or more means round up.

39
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:33,260
Step 4: for whole numbers, fill the places with zeros, up to the decimal point.

40
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:36,740
Round 0.004836 to 3 significant figures.

41
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:39,690
The first significant figure is 4.

42
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:41,510
Count three: 4, 8, 3.

43
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:44,930
The next digit is 6, so round up.

44
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:50,400
So the answer is 0.00484, to 3 significant figures.

45
00:02:50,450 --> 00:02:51,240
Your turn.

46
00:02:51,290 --> 00:02:54,350
Round 2.645 to 2 significant figures.

47
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:57,600
Pause and work it out.

48
00:02:57,650 --> 00:03:01,050
The first two significant figures are 2 and 6.

49
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:04,050
The next digit is 4, so do not round up.

50
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,950
The answer is 2.6.

51
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,050
Round 7.997 to 3 significant figures.

52
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:14,710
The digits are 7, 9, 9, and the next digit is 7, so round up.

53
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:16,780
7.99 plus 0.01 is 8.

54
00:03:16,830 --> 00:03:21,680
To show 3 significant figures, write 8.00.

55
00:03:21,730 --> 00:03:26,690
Rounding to 1 significant figure is good for estimating.

56
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:29,570
Estimate 62.4 times 0.487.

57
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,660
62.4 is about 60.

58
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:34,000
0.487 is about 0.5.

59
00:03:34,050 --> 00:03:36,890
60 times 0.5 is 30.

60
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:41,210
Lena rounds 0.003527 to 2 significant figures.

61
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:43,640
Which line is wrong?

62
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:44,790
Line 1 is wrong.

63
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:47,890
The zeros at the front are not significant.

64
00:03:47,940 --> 00:03:50,900
The first significant figure is 3.

65
00:03:50,950 --> 00:03:53,190
The first two are 3 and 5.

66
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,960
The next digit is 2.

67
00:03:55,010 --> 00:03:57,630
So the answer is 0.0035.

68
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:00,240
News reports round big numbers.

69
00:04:00,290 --> 00:04:06,970
If 61,847 people watch a football match, a report might say about 62,000 people.

70
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:10,050
That is 2 significant figures.

71
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:13,430
A human hair is about 0.07 millimetres thick.

72
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:19,230
That is 1 significant figure, and it is accurate enough for most uses.

73
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:20,680
One last question.

74
00:04:20,730 --> 00:04:26,650
Estimate 19.7 times 41.2, by rounding each number to 1 significant figure.

75
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:30,230
Pause the video and answer.

76
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:32,390
19.7 is about 20.

77
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,560
41.2 is about 40.

78
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:37,530
20 times 40 is 800.

79
00:04:37,580 --> 00:04:43,330
To remember: the first significant figure is the first digit that is not zero.

80
00:04:43,380 --> 00:04:45,190
Zeros between digits count.

81
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:48,430
Zeros at the front of a decimal do not.

82
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:53,360
Round as usual, then fill with zeros to keep the size of whole numbers.

83
00:04:53,410 --> 00:04:57,090
Round to 1 significant figure to estimate.

84
00:04:57,140 --> 00:05:02,270
Great work! Now practise lesson 3.2 on Camday.
